# Expo's Metro bundler cannot resolve pnpm's default symlinked node_modules layout
# (it doesn't follow the symlinks pnpm uses to save disk space), so Metro fails to
# find packages that are actually installed. Flat/hoisted node_modules (npm/yarn
# classic style) is what makes `apps/mobile` bundle at all.
#
# NOTE: as of pnpm 11, the setting that controls this (`nodeLinker`) lives in
# pnpm-workspace.yaml, not here — pnpm dropped .npmrc's `node-linker` key. This
# file is kept for the other per-registry / auth settings that still belong in
# .npmrc, and so this comment is where someone looking for "why hoisted?" finds
# the answer and a pointer to where the actual setting now lives.
# See docs/architecture/2026-08-09-initial-architecture-proposal.md §1.2.
